Ground speed = distance ÷ time  

\[
\text{Time} = 1\ \text{hour}\;30\ \text{minutes}=1.5\ \text{hours}
\]

\[
\text{Speed}= \frac{450\ \text{nautical miles}}{1.5\ \text{hours}}
           = 300\ \text{knots}
\]

So the plane’s ground speed is **300 knots**.
